From 6e4644e0d4b000da827688f68d769daa83542ffd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 07:53:18 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Add optional vocal restoration (VoiceFixer, Resemble Enhance)
 and pitch smoothing

- audio_restore.py runs each restorer in an isolated, version-pinned sidecar
  environment so their dependencies cannot conflict with Applio's stack.
  Transitive versions are frozen to a date, results are cached on disk, and
  Resemble Enhance installs without its unused training dependencies.
- Restoration runs at the file's native sample rate before resampling.
- New --restore-mode, --restore-nfe/solver/lambd/tau and --f0-smooth CLI
  options, plus a Vocal restoration panel in the single-file tab.
- f0 median smoothing runs inside each voiced run so voicing is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015KE1esskP9ysQXNHcQWpEW
